   This image is not Apache-2.0 as a whole. Only the Fadenstack runtime
   helper in /opt/llm-port/runtime is. The rest keeps its own terms,
   which travel with it:

   - The GB10 image is built on vLLM's own image (vllm/vllm-openai,
     Apache-2.0). The x86_64 image is built on a Python base image, with
     vLLM, PyTorch and Ray installed from PyPI.
   - Both contain NVIDIA software as their upstream projects and NVIDIA's
     own Python packages distribute it:
     * CUDA libraries and related Python packages (nvidia-*), under the
       CUDA EULA and their own licences;
     * NVIDIA developer tools (ptxas, nvcc, nvdisasm, cuobjdump), which
       vLLM's base image, PyTorch, Triton and NVIDIA's Python packages
       include to compile GPU code while models run, under the CUDA EULA;
     * the NVIDIA CUTLASS DSL (nvidia-cutlass-dsl), a dependency of vLLM,
       under its own licence, the NVIDIA CUTLASS DSL EULA.
     Their licence files are in their site-packages folders and, in the
     GB10 image, under /usr/local/cuda*.
   - Ray, vLLM and the other open-source packages keep their licences;
     their files are in their site-packages folders.

   Under review: NVIDIA's terms do not expressly grant redistribution of
   some of these components. The CUDA EULA's list of distributable files
   (Attachment A) does not name the developer tools above, and the CUTLASS
   DSL's licence grants distribution of its Python source files only.
   Large open-source inference projects distribute these components in
   the same way, and the question has been raised publicly without an
   answer from NVIDIA so far (for example
   https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/1618).

   Based on the information available, we are reviewing this and will
   seek clarification from NVIDIA. If the review confirms that a
   component may not be redistributed in this image, we will remove it
   from future images and change how it reaches the GPU machines, for
   example by having them download it from NVIDIA directly. Fadenstack is
   pre-1.0 software in active testing. Rights holders who have concerns
   about a component in this image can write to contact@emagin8.de; we
   will respond promptly.

